## 1. Introduction to Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) in Java & Boilerplate
- **Boilerplate Code**: The standard structural skeleton required to run a Java program.
- **Class Definition (`Student`)**: 
  - Represents a blueprint or a template for real-world entities.
  - Contains **Attributes/Characteristics** (represented as variables) and **Behaviours** (represented as functions/methods).

```java
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;
    int rollNumber;
    String college;

    void markAttendance() {
        System.out.println("Attendance marked for student: " + name);
    }
}
```

