## 6. Practical Exam & Interview Technical Warnings

1. **Parameter Mismatch Error in `equals` Override:**
   ```java
   // WRONG: This OVERLOADS the method, does not OVERRIDE it.
   @Override // Compilation Error!
   public boolean equals(Student s) { 
       return this.name == s.name;
   }
   ```
   *Correction:* Always define the parameter type as `Object obj`.

2. **`println` Auto-Conversion:** 
   `System.out.println(obj)` implicitly executes `obj.toString()`. Overriding `toString()` alters the console output of `System.out.println(obj)` directly.

3. **Default Equality Behavior:** 
   Until overridden, `obj1.equals(obj2)` is functionally identical to `obj1 == obj2`.


---

### Complete Optimized `equals()` Implementation Algorithm

```java
@Override
public boolean equals(Object obj) {
    // 1. Reference Check (Performance Optimization)
    if (this == obj) {
        return true;
    }

    // 2. Null Check (Prevents NullPointerException)
    if (obj == null) {
        return false;
    }

    // 3. Class Type Check (Prevents ClassCastException)
    if (obj.getClass() != this.getClass()) {
        return false;
    }

    // 4. Typecast after safety checks
    Student s = (Student) obj;

    // 5. Field-by-Field Comparison
    return this.age == s.age && 
           (this.name == s.name || (this.name != null && this.name.equals(s.name)));
}
```

